# Rust build output: compiled artifacts and incremental build cache.
# Regenerated by `cargo build`/`cargo run` — never worth committing.
/target/
**/target/
# Debug symbol files rustc/MSVC can emit on Windows builds.
*.pdb

# Editor/IDE project settings — local to each contributor's setup, except
# settings.json: it carries watcher/search excludes for the huge reference/
# checkouts below, which every contributor needs, not just personal prefs.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
# Vim swap files left behind by an unclean exit.
*.swp
*.swo
# Generic editor backup files (e.g. Emacs auto-save-on-write).
*~

# OS-generated metadata files, not part of the project.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local environment files that may hold secrets/config — never commit these.
.env
.env.local

# Runtime log output.
*.log

# External reference source checkouts (Gecko, Chromium, V8) — large,
# third-party, not our code. Never committed; only specific ported files
# (with the CONTRIBUTING.md header conventions) get copied out and added
# to the repo. See development/browser_core/reference/README.md.
/development/browser_core/reference/gecko/
/development/browser_core/reference/chromium/
/development/browser_core/reference/v8/
